{"name":"Total Eclipse","hex":"#303543","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"total eclipse","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An eclipse in which the eclipsed body is completely obscured to the viewer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/total_eclipse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Total Eclipse (American band)","blocks":[{"text":"Total Eclipse is an American metal band from San Francisco, California, with a self-produced mini-CD released internationally, a worldwide album released under a major record label, Spellcaster Kukulkan in 2013. In 2021, the band released an album, Enemy Enemy, independently. In 2025 the band issued the remastered version of Kukulcan and the live compilation The Live Metal Project. https://totaleclipse2.bandcamp.com/album/kukulcan-remastered"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_Eclipse_(American_band)"},{"title":"Total Eclipse (web series)","blocks":[{"text":"Total Eclipse is an American teen drama television series starring Mackenzie Ziegler, Lauren Orlando, Johnny Orlando, Emily Skinner, Nadia Turner, Devenity Perkins, and Darius Marcell. The series is produced by digital network Brat and premiered on April 5, 2018, on Brat's YouTube channel. It follows a group of high school students and sheds light on common themes among teens such as bullying and relationships, including friendships, cliques, and romances. The protagonist Cassie, played by Ziegler, is cast out of her childhood friend circle and seeks to re-establish those friendships, make new friends, and negotiate social situations at school and in her community."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/TotalEclipse3.jpg/330px-TotalEclipse3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_Eclipse_(web_series)"},{"title":"Eclipse","blocks":[{"text":"An eclipse is an astronomical event which occurs when an astronomical object or spacecraft is temporarily obscured, by passing into the shadow of another body or by having another body pass between it and the viewer. This alignment of three celestial objects is known as a syzygy. An eclipse is the result of either an occultation or a transit. A \"deep eclipse\" is when a small astronomical object is behind a bigger one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg/330px-Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eclipse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/TotalEclipse3.jpg/330px-TotalEclipse3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/TotalEclipse3.jpg/330px-TotalEclipse3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATotalEclipse3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg/500px-Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg/1280px-Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg/500px-Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Totality during the solar eclipse of August 11, 1999, showing the solar corona and prominences","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASolar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/ISS-52_Eclipse_2017_Umbra_Viewed_from_Space_%281%29.jpg/500px-ISS-52_Eclipse_2017_Umbra_Viewed_from_Space_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=